module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.receipt_subject_is_the_prose_about_the_mechanism

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, decl_ref }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data receipt_subject_is_the_prose_about_the_mechanism: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "receipt_subject_is_the_prose_about_the_mechanism" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a behavioral receipt is built correctly -- fault injection, positive control, typed refusal -- around a subject that is the DOCUMENTATION of the mechanism rather than the mechanism** (INVALID STATE: a module's equivalence receipt compares a declaration whose content is a description of what the module does, so the receipt is green, discriminating, and would not move if every behavior it purports to cover were deleted. ",

    "HARM: this is worse than an absent receipt and worse than a weak one. ",

    "An absent receipt is counted as absent; a weak receipt fails an adversarial read. ",

    "This one passes every structural check a reviewer applies to receipts -- it HAS a discriminating fault arm, it HAS a positive control, it refuses when the arm fires -- so it is enrolled, cited as the module's behavioral coverage, and it satisfies the frontier row that says the module is receipted. ",

    "The mechanism it covers is exactly nothing. ",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS. The tell is not the receipt's shape, which is why shape review misses it: it is the ARITY AND TYPE of the case list. ",

    "One case, of type String, whose name ends in note/law/doc/rationale, is the signature. ",

    "It is distinct from an inert lens (the receipt executes), from rung inflation in prose (the claim here is machine-checked, it just checks the wrong subject), and from a stale coverage sentence (nothing here is stale -- the comparison is live and correct about a string). ",

    "SPECIMEN, and it is on the compiler's own front door. ",

    "The self-host behavioral receipt for `v2.compiler.compile` -- `gunbc/instruments/self_host_00_compile_shims/witness_main.rs` -- carries a case list of exactly one entry, `required_lens_grain_note`, compared between the emitted crate and the seed. ",

    "That declaration is the prose describing the two required-lens roster grains. ",

    "The seed side of the comparison, `v1_compiler::v2_compiler_compile`, is a nine-line Rust module whose entire content is that same string. ",

    "So the strongest verdict the emitted crate can publish about the compile door is that two copies of a sentence about lenses agree, while the door's eight enrolled gates, its lens fold, its subtree walk and its rejection path are all outside the receipt's subject. ",

    "WHY THE SHAPE IS RIGHT AND THE SUBJECT IS NOT, stated together because the shape is what earns the receipt its standing: the shim takes `--inject-fault`, substitutes a wrong value on case zero, and exits non-zero -- a real discriminating arm over a real positive control. ",

    "Every one of those properties survives if the subject is a constant. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable, and specifically NOT the mechanically-preventable rung the receipt's enrolment implies. ",

    "CEILING: mechanically preventable. ",

    "A receipt's subject set is a fact about the shim that a reader can derive -- the declarations it names -- and the property that at least one of them is reached by the module's own behavior is checkable. ",

    "It is not structurally guaranteeable, because whether a declaration is the mechanism or a description of it is not decidable in general. ",

    "NEXT TRIGGER: the behavioral-receipt frontier requires each module's receipt to name at least one subject that is a function rather than a data declaration, and refuses a receipt whose whole case list is data -- at which point this specimen refuses and the compile door's receipt has to acquire a real subject rather than being counted as covered.)"
  ],

  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "v2.compiler.compile", decl_name: "required_lens_grain_note"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "v2.compiler.compile", decl_name: "validate_then_compile"),
    decl_ref(
      module_path: "gunbc.guarantee_stall.self_host_wet_route_receipt_lifetime_stall",
      decl_name: "self_host_wet_route_receipt_lifetime_stall"
    ),
    decl_ref(
      module_path: "gunbc.v2_compile_obligation_census",
      decl_name: "native_standing"
    ),
  ],
}
